    "result_text": "Everything is verified and consistent. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field. The build passes with the test green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\nA live example from the audit log confirms the format: `NSW2716E6609E1` = `NSW` (region from postcode) + `27` (FY, since 2026\u201108\u201111 is in the fiscal year ending 2027) + `16E6609E` (8 upper\u2011hex of SHA\u2011256 over telephone+lastName) + `1` (Luhn check digit over `NSW2716E6609E`, which I verified independently equals 1).\n\nChanges made:\n\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 replaced the `customer_code`/`customerCode` field (and accessors) with `member_id`/`memberId`.\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 renamed the `customer_code` column to `member_id` (widened to `VARCHAR(30)` to accommodate the longer id plus any collision suffix).\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `checkDigit` schema properties with a single read\u2011only `memberId` property (regenerates the DTO).\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 dropped the `membershipNumber`/`checkDigit` mappings and methods (`memberId` now auto-maps from the entity); rewrote `locality` and `fiscalYear` to derive their region and fiscal\u2011year segments from the `memberId`; and updated the `OwnerFieldsDto` reverse mapping to ignore `memberId`.\n- **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 replaced `customerCode(...)`/`deduplicateCustomerCode(...)` with `memberId(...)`/`deduplicateMemberId(...)` (adding `fiscalYearEnding` and `luhnCheckDigit` helpers); collision handling now applies to the memberId; `primaryIdentifier` returns the memberId; and both audit records (the human\u2011readable line and the structured `OwnerCreatedEvent` JSON) now carry `memberId`.\n\nThe `ownerSegment` already derives through `locality`, which now reads from the memberId, so it references the memberId as required.\n\nNote: I updated the four `schema.sql` files, but they're only loaded fresh into the in\u2011memory test/dev databases. If you have an existing persistent MySQL/Postgres database, it would need a migration (`ALTER TABLE owners RENAME COLUMN customer_code TO member_id` plus a widening) \u2014 let me know if you'd like me to add one.",
